    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "One popular approach when considering possible experimental designs is to compute the sample size required to give the expected confidence interval a preset length, so that the interval given by $ \\mu_1 \\pm z_\\alpha f_1 / \\sqrt{n} $ does not include $ \\mu_0 $. Here $ z_\\alpha $ is the appropriate value to give an $ \\alpha $-level one- or two-sided test (depending on the hypothesis being tested). Solving for $ n $,",
